{title: 218 - When He Cometh}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F#m]When He cometh, when He [A7/G]cometh To [F#m]make up His [G]jewels,
[D/A]All His [Em/G]jewels, [D/F#]precious jewels, His loved and [A7/G]His own.
[F#m]Like the stars of [G]the morning, [D]His bright crown [Em/G]adorning,
[F#m]They shall shine [G]in their [Bm]beauty, [D]Bright gems [F#m]for His [D/F#]crown.

Refrain:
[D/F#]Like the [A]stars of [D/A]the morning,
[F#m]His brightness [G]adorning,
[D]They shall shine in [G]their beauty,
[D/F#]Bright gems [Em/G]for His [D/F#]crown.

Verse 2:
[F#m]He will gather, [A7/G]He [F#m]will gather
[D/A]The [Em/G]gems [D/F#]for His kingdom;
[F#m]All the pure [G]ones, [D]all the bright [Em/G]ones,
[F#m]His [G]loved [Bm]and [D]His [F#m]own.

Verse 3:
[F#m]Little children, [A7/G]little [F#m]children,
[D/A]Who [Em/G]love [D/F#]their Redeemer,
[F#m]Are the jewels, [D]precious [Em/G]jewels,
[F#m]His [G]loved [Bm]and [D]His [F#m]own.
